 "is_vocab": false,
 "stimulus_html": "The apportionment of 70 new emergency blue lights in three parking lots is based on acreage. The standard quota for each lot is listed in the table below. Use this information to answer each question.\n<table class=\"unnumbered\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Lot</th>\n<th>Acres</th>\n<th>Lot’s Standard Quota</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>A</td>\n<td>15</td>\n<td> <span data-math=\"15 \\div 0.4857 \\approx 30.88\">15 \\div 0.4857 \\approx 30.88</span> emergency blue lights</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>B</td>\n<td>9</td>\n<td> <span data-math=\"9 \\div 0.4857 \\approx 18.53\">9 \\div 0.4857 \\approx 18.53</span> emergency blue lights</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>C</td>\n<td>10</td>\n<td> <span data-math=\"10 \\div 0.4857 = 20.59\">10 \\div 0.4857 = 20.59</span> emergency blue lights</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 545175,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Give the lower quota for each parking lot.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The total population <span data-math=\"{\\text{ =  15  +  9  +  10  =  34}}\"></span> acres</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"{\\text{Standard Divisor = }}\\frac{{{\\text{Total Population}}}}{{{\\text{House Size}}}} = \\frac{{{\\text{34 acres}}}}{{{\\text{70 lights}}}} \\approx 0.4857{\\text{ acres per light}}\"></span></p>\n<p>Hamilton’s method is to always round down, which results in the lower quota.</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Lot</th>\n<th><span data-math=\"{\\text{Standard Quota = }}\\frac{{{\\text{State Population}}}}{{{\\text{Standard Divisor}}}}{\\text{ }}\"></span></th>\n<th>Lower Quota</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>A</td>\n<td><span data-math=\"\\frac{{{\\text{15 acres}}}}{{0.4857{\\text{ acres per light}}}}{\\text{ = 30}}{\\text{.88 lights}}\"></span></td>\n<td>30</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>B</td>\n<td><span data-math=\"\\frac{{{\\text{9 acres}}}}{{0.4857{\\text{ acres per light}}}}{\\text{ = 18}}{\\text{.53 lights}}\"></span></td>\n<td>18</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>C</td>\n<td><span data-math=\"\\frac{{{\\text{10 acres}}}}{{0.4857{\\text{ acres per light}}}}{\\text{ = 20}}{\\text{.59 lights}}\"></span></td>\n<td>20</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "30, 18, 20"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
